## std.debug — panic primitive.
##
## `panic(msg)` aborts the process via the always-emitted
## `__zag_panic` preamble shim (src/codegen/core.zig → 1-arg
## convenience over `__zag_panic_at`, which writes "panic: <msg>" to
## stderr and @trap()s).
##
## v0.1 Tier-1 migration: the pre-migration `builtin_panic` router
## row emitted `__zag_panic_at(msg, "<source path>", line, col)`
## with the call site's exact zag location. A library function
## cannot know its caller's source position, so the .zag body posts
## a sentinel "<generated>" location — the trade-off is documented
## in the preamble shim. `assert(cond)` keeps its compiler-router
## shape (it still threads the call-site location through
## `__zag_panic_at`).

pub fun panic(msg: str) {
    __zag_panic(msg);
}
